    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d190">

                <pb facs="0359" n="227" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg227"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/6–2345: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 190 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d190-f1"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-06T18:00:00-04:00">July 6, 1945—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5517. …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>You may accordingly tell FonOff that … at forthcoming highest-level discussions
                    we intend to press strongly proposals for implementation of Yalta
                        Declaration<anchor n="2" xml:id="d190-f2"/> and reorganization of ACC’s in
                    all three ex-satellites. We shall oppose proposals to establish diplomatic
                    relations or conclude peace with present Govts there. …</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d190-f1" n="1" xml:id="d190-f1-content">
                <p>For the full text of this message, see <ref target="#d303">document No.
                    303</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d190-f2" n="2" xml:id="d190-f2-content">
                <p>On Liberated Europe. See <ref target="frus1945Berlinv02#d1417">vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, document No. 1417, section <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">v</hi>
                    </ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
